{"cases":[{"attack":true,"case":"The target asserts that sustained flags are justified by 'cross-critic consistency across independently seeded falsificationist stances (SRC_007, SRC_009)' — yet the target itself lists zero commitments ('commitments: (none)'). Under §11.3 the adjudication ritual requires sustained flags to be bound to adjudicative commitments that can be checked; pointing to agreement between two other critics is a rhetorical appeal to consensus, not the commitment-grounded justification the ritual standard demands. The target therefore explains the wrong thing: it argues 'other critics agree' instead of stating the ritual commitment under which the flags are sustained.","counterexample":["A target that said: 'The flags under §11.3 are sustained because each flagged item violates the explicit falsifiability commitment requiring a stated counterexample condition — a binding commitment of this adjudicator.'"],"premise":"§11.3 sustained flags must be justified by the adjudicator's own commitment schema, not by appeal to agreement among external critics.","target":"64ddcd4cf443ebe1a1350698153951201b51338833c7709ced49c4369a9c9fb2"}]}